02:18.880 --> 02:20.500
Okay, all!

02:20.500 --> 02:22.640
Today will be the start of a long break,

02:22.640 --> 02:26.490
and I doubt you have much 
left to do for this year,

02:26.490 --> 02:31.240
so once you've cleaned up your 
desk area, you can go right home.

02:33.750 --> 02:37.510
Did the president seem a bit tired to you?

02:37.510 --> 02:38.710
She did.

02:38.710 --> 02:42.610
As a nurarihyon descendant, 
she loves "night parade"-style activities,

02:42.610 --> 02:46.010
so I assumed she'd throw 
a big end-of-year party.

02:46.550 --> 02:51.680
Apparently she burned out her 
"night parade" energy at Christmas!

02:51.680 --> 02:55.520
What in the world happened 
while we were skiing?

02:56.210 --> 02:58.660
If you have any documents
 you don't need, give 'em to me.

02:58.660 --> 03:00.700
I'll take them to the shredder.

03:02.240 --> 03:04.530
Could you take these, then?

03:04.530 --> 03:05.760
Sure.

03:05.760 --> 03:07.440
Thank you very much.

03:09.050 --> 03:11.550
This... is from that time 
we worked overtime together.

03:13.790 --> 03:15.250
<b></b>Checking

03:13.790 --> 03:15.250
<b></b>Later

03:13.790 --> 03:15.250
<b></b>Call back

03:13.790 --> 03:15.250
<b></b>Wait a while longer

03:16.090 --> 03:17.540
You're throwing this out, too?

03:17.850 --> 03:20.040
I would never throw that out!

03:20.340 --> 03:23.800
<i>I'm gonna pass that one down 
to my descendants!</i>

03:27.200 --> 03:29.800
Aren't you two cozy?

03:32.810 --> 03:35.810
<b></b>Kannondori Street

03:36.060 --> 03:38.390
It seems we made it through another year.

03:38.390 --> 03:39.320
Yes.

03:49.020 --> 03:51.080
You didn't bring gloves?

03:51.080 --> 03:52.820
I forgot today.

03:52.820 --> 03:54.190
I'm so cold...

03:54.190 --> 03:57.950
<i>A snow woman descendant gets cold hands?</i>

03:58.310 --> 04:00.320
Are you all right without gloves?

04:01.080 --> 04:02.830
I'm quite warm.

04:03.330 --> 04:07.910
There's a saying, "Cold hands, warm heart."

04:08.320 --> 04:11.850
It's a bit uncomfortable to consider, 
but the opposite may be true, as well.

04:12.160 --> 04:13.930
No, no, no, no!

04:13.930 --> 04:16.000
You're a very kind person.

04:16.000 --> 04:18.610
That's just a superstition.

04:18.610 --> 04:20.690
You're very, very kind!

04:26.170 --> 04:27.370
Well, then...

04:29.150 --> 04:33.380
The very kind Fuyutsuki-san 
will share some of her warmth.

04:35.200 --> 04:36.370
If I may.

04:41.280 --> 04:42.230
<i>Eh?</i>

04:44.330 --> 04:47.020
Hey, they're holding hands!

04:47.020 --> 04:49.090
They're good friends, huh?

04:49.780 --> 04:50.960
They certainly are!

04:50.780 --> 04:51.790
I'm sorry.

04:51.790 --> 04:54.270
N-N-Not at all...

04:58.420 --> 05:01.020
<i>We freakin' held hands!</i>

05:04.280 --> 05:07.640
At New Year's time, 
you gotta clean your snow hut!

05:08.280 --> 05:14.520
Of course, we gotta build 
a snow hut before we clean it!

05:14.520 --> 05:17.600
Huh? And what's icicle makeup, you ask?

05:17.600 --> 05:19.300
Heh, heh, heh.

05:19.300 --> 05:21.800
<i>You... will... see!</i>

05:22.660 --> 05:24.920
She's as inscrutable as always.

05:26.380 --> 05:28.550
Guess I should clean out my room, too.

05:31.690 --> 05:34.640
Not that there's not much cleaning to do...

05:34.640 --> 05:36.560
I keep pretty clean, anyway.

05:38.560 --> 05:41.160
No work for a while...

05:42.080 --> 05:45.320
I might not see Fuyutsuki-san 'til the new year.

05:45.320 --> 05:46.820
Big Bro!

05:47.680 --> 05:48.900
Learn to knock, dang it!

05:48.900 --> 05:51.210
I need your help with a stream!

05:51.210 --> 05:52.820
What kind of help?!

05:53.240 --> 05:55.500
I'm doing a New Year's Eve stream,

05:55.500 --> 06:00.200
and my plan was to melt one snowman 
for each ring of the New Year's bell.

06:00.570 --> 06:02.840
So can I have 108 snowmen?

06:02.840 --> 06:04.590
They ain't that easy to make!

06:04.860 --> 06:05.590
Here.

06:08.100 --> 06:10.520
Oh, Fuyutsuki-san's so cute...

06:10.520 --> 06:11.160
Adorable!

06:11.160 --> 06:11.840
Cute!

06:11.840 --> 06:13.840
See? Snowmen on demand!

06:13.840 --> 06:15.510
Respect your big brother!

06:16.100 --> 06:17.230
<b></b>Komori-san
You have a new message.

06:18.510 --> 06:20.600
Hey, is it from Fuyutsuki-san?

06:23.600 --> 06:26.180
I can do my cleaning tomorrow.

06:26.180 --> 06:27.720
Right, Nyamero?

06:33.240 --> 06:36.250
<b></b>See you again tomorrow.

06:33.240 --> 06:36.250
<b></b>Yes, I'll see you then.

06:33.240 --> 06:36.250
<b></b>12/29

06:33.240 --> 06:36.250
<b></b>Would you like to join us for
 an online New Year's Eve party?

06:36.240 --> 06:38.470
<i>Yeah!</i>

06:38.500 --> 06:38.620
<b>Chuhai</b>

06:38.500 --> 06:40.500
<b></b>Komori

06:38.620 --> 06:38.750
<b>Chuhai</b>

06:38.750 --> 06:38.870
<b>Chuhai</b>

06:38.800 --> 06:40.490
<i>Cheers, all!</i>

06:38.870 --> 06:39.000
<b>Chuhai</b>

06:39.000 --> 06:39.120
<b>Chuhai</b>

06:39.120 --> 06:40.500
<b>Chuhai</b>

